  <prompt>
    Execute Track-B batch 1 of FR-TB-01 (sweep-as-you-go): delete the DirectOpenAiAgent cluster and its dependents plus the server-side dependency-free deadwood from inventory §9 / the migration map's start-now delete list. These files are dead by definition — `DirectOpenAiAgent` is registered at `AiChatModule.cs:61` but never consumed, and its test suite maintains dead code. This batch rides alongside wave W-P0-A because it has zero overlap with live-code tasks. Per NFR-08 (hard-cutover proof), every deletion must be grep-zero-verified with SHOWN output, and builds must be proven green. Batch evidence lands in `notes/track-b/batch-1-evidence.md`.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    .NET developer disciplined at surgical dead-code removal in the Sprk.Bff.Api codebase — verifies liveness before deleting, shows grep evidence, and never widens a delete beyond the batch list.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Every batch-1 item below is deleted (or recorded keep-with-reason if found live), grep returns zero hits per deleted symbol outside git history (output shown), `dotnet build` is green (output shown), TASK-INDEX is updated, and `notes/track-b/batch-1-evidence.md` is written.
  </goal>

  <inputs>
    <file purpose="design-spec">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/spec.md</file>
    <file purpose="project-plan">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/plan.md</file>
    <file purpose="project-context">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
    <file purpose="task-index">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md</file>
    <file purpose="deadwood-register">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/notes/audit-inputs/SPAARKE-AI-CODE-INVENTORY.md</file>
    <file purpose="delete-list">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/notes/audit-inputs/SPAARKE-AI-MIGRATION-MAP.md</file>
  </inputs>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Do not modify files outside the batch list; deadwood only — if a batch item turns out to be live, STOP and record keep-with-reason in the batch evidence file instead of deleting.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-08">Every retirement verified grep-zero with SHOWN output in the transcript and in the evidence file; no compat shims retained.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">`PlaybookDispatcher` and `CompoundIntentDetector` FILES delete at P2 (task 035) — this batch removes ONLY the dead method `RunPhaseBManifestPresentAsync` and the dead assignment (lines 97-98) respectively. Do not delete those files here.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029 / NFR-01">Deletions are expected to reduce or hold publish size; report any anomaly.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Deleting `DirectOpenAiAgentTests` is removal of a test-of-dead-code (SCAFFOLDING class) — record it in the evidence file for the task-090 /test-diet reconciliation.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>bff-api/dead-code-removal, track-b</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/plan.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/notes/audit-inputs/SPAARKE-AI-MIGRATION-MAP.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/notes/audit-inputs/SPAARKE-AI-CODE-INVENTORY.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/notes/audit-inputs/OVERLAY-MATRIX.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <context>
    <background>
      FR-TB-01 distributes the migration map's ~30 dependency-free deletes across four batches riding phase waves. Batch 1 is the server cluster. Batch contents (inventory §9 "Server" + migration-map start-now list):
      (1) `DirectOpenAiAgent` + `ISprkAgent` + DTOs (`AgentRequest`, `ConversationTurn`) — registered `AiChatModule.cs:61`, never consumed;
      (2) the `AiChatModule.cs:61` DI registration line (dependent edit in a live file);
      (3) `DirectOpenAiAgentTests` (test maintaining dead code);
      (4) `Services/Ai/Chat/SseEvent.cs`;
      (5) `ScopeGapDetector` (no DI registration);
      (6) `DocumentVectorBackfillService` (one-time migration, stub method);
      (7) `SummarizeInvocationPath.AgentTool` enum value;
      (8) `PlaybookDispatcher.RunPhaseBManifestPresentAsync` (unreachable scaffolding — method only, file deletes at P2);
      (9) `LinearConsumersOptions.ActionIds` residue;
      (10) `CompoundIntentDetector` dead assignment at lines 97-98 (file itself deletes at P2).
    </background>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="none" status="complete">No dependencies — rides wave W-P0-A from project start.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
    <related-work>
      <item>Task 050 (FR-P4-01) audits every §9 item at P4 — this batch's evidence file feeds that audit table</item>
      <item>Task 035 (FR-P2-06) deletes PlaybookDispatcher + CompoundIntentDetector files at P2</item>
    </related-work>
  </context>

  <steps>
    <step order="0" name="Context check">
      Check context usage. If &gt; 70%, create handoff summary and request new chat. Load inputs; read inventory §9 (Server) and migration map Track-B list.
    </step>
    <step order="1" name="Read and confirm the batch list">
      Locate every batch-1 item via Glob/Grep (exact file paths + all reference sites). For each item, confirm deadness: no production consumer outside the cluster itself. If any item is live, mark it keep-with-reason and exclude from deletion.
    </step>
    <step order="2" name="Delete the batch">
      Delete the confirmed-dead files; remove the `AiChatModule.cs:61` registration, the `SummarizeInvocationPath.AgentTool` enum value, the `RunPhaseBManifestPresentAsync` method, the `ActionIds` residue, and the CompoundIntentDetector dead assignment. Touch nothing else in those live files.
    </step>
    <step order="3" name="Grep-zero verification (SHOWN)">
      For each deleted symbol (`DirectOpenAiAgent`, `ISprkAgent`, `AgentRequest` (agent DTO), `ConversationTurn`, `SseEvent`, `ScopeGapDetector`, `DocumentVectorBackfillService`, `AgentTool`, `RunPhaseBManifestPresentAsync`, `ActionIds`): run grep across src/ + tests/ and SHOW the zero-hit output in the transcript. Note any intentional survivor (e.g., unrelated same-name symbols) explicitly.
    </step>
    <step order="4" name="Build verification (SHOWN)">
      Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` and `dotnet test` for the touched test project; show green output. No client surface is touched in this batch — npm build not required unless grep in step 3 reveals client references.
    </step>
    <step order="5" name="Evidence + close">
      Write `projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/notes/track-b/batch-1-evidence.md` (item table: deleted-path / grep output / keep-with-reason). Update TASK-INDEX.md (070 → ✅). Report completion.
    </step>
  </steps>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build + test verification</tool>
    <tool name="git">Version control (deletions preserved in history)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ (batch-1 deletions incl. AiChatModule.cs registration removal)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ (DirectOpenAiAgentTests deleted)</output>
    <output type="report">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/notes/track-b/batch-1-evidence.md</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarke-ai-architecture-redesign-r1/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md (status update)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Per-batch grep-zero for every deleted symbol outside git history, with output SHOWN (FR-TB-01 / NFR-08).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build + touched test suites green with output shown.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Any live-found item is recorded keep-with-reason instead of deleted; no files outside the batch list modified.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">notes/track-b/batch-1-evidence.md exists with the per-item evidence table; TASK-INDEX updated.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
